 "applies_to": "Schneider Electric APC InRow RC ACRC100-series in-row coolers on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
 "summary": "Gateway profile for the APC InRow RC ACRC100 series: 111 objects (85 AI, 26 AO), all polled. Outputs set cooling and supply air setpoints, fan speed preference and limits, PID terms, glycol %, thresholds and startup/idle options; inputs give overall and group status, operate mode, cool output and demand, rack inlet, supply and return temperatures, airflow, containment and filter pressure, fluid valve, flow and temperatures, run hours and the alarm flags.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile HI_LO_APC_InRow_RC_ACRC100Series_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the InRow RC ACRC100 Modbus register map (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/MLAN-7NHMSU_R2_EN.pdf).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "All 111 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
  "Contemporary Controls ships two CSVs in the ZIP (HI_LO and LO_HI word order) with the same objects and instances; pick the one that matches the unit's float word order."
 ],
